QUERY: rg -n -i '^description:.*(requirement|objective|diagnostic|observab|fixed.*decomposition|bounded.*adapt)' kb/sources/ --glob *.md --glob !*.brief.md
kb/sources/popper-epistemology-without-a-knowing-subject-1968.ingest.md:2:description: "Popper distinguishes objective conjectural contents from acts of thought and linguistic forms, making criticism central to learning without equating it with formalization."
kb/sources/harness-engineering-for-self-improvement.ingest.md:2:description: "Harness self-improvement synthesis separates editable deployment machinery from the model, but its benchmark evidence remains bounded by fixed objectives, evaluators, and outer loops"
kb/sources/continual-harness-online-adaptation-foundation-agents.ingest.md:2:description: "Continual Harness adds a reset-free all-three-form learning case, bounded by direct edit adoption, low artifact reuse, and a fixed embodied-game decomposition"
kb/sources/adam-mastroianni-infinite-midwit.ingest.md:2:description: Objective-vs-subjective intelligence essay arguing that AI's real bottleneck is taste and boringness judgment, not benchmarked competence
kb/sources/optimal-choice-of-hypothesis-is-the-weakest-not-the-shortest.ingest.md:2:description: "Bennett's extension-size alternative to minimum description length, bounded by its uniform task prior and fixed representational decomposition"
kb/sources/kennedy-sobek-kennedy-set-based-rework.ingest.md:2:description: "Set-based requirements, targeted experiments, and evidence-gated convergence are proposed as remedies for three causes of late systems-engineering rework."
kb/sources/wikiskill-persistent-knowledge-for-skill-evolution.ingest.md:2:description: "WikiSkill improves skill evolution with a persistent diagnostic wiki; its ablations distinguish proposer memory from solver access while leaving wiki claims outside validation gating."
kb/sources/harnessdev-llms-create-and-evolve-agent-harnesses.ingest.md:2:description: "HarnessDev provides bounded evidence that harness quality depends on executor fit, diagnostic use, evaluation noise, and the fixed development regime."
kb/sources/einstein-brownian-motion-1905.ingest.md:2:description: "Einstein derives observable particle displacement from molecular theory; a historical comparison for discriminating predictions and preserving evidential status."
kb/sources/arrmlet-tracecraft.ingest.md:2:description: S3-backed CLI coordination tool for multi-agent systems — exposes how file-backed coordination depends on workload-specific consistency and authority requirements
kb/sources/sean-goedecke-what-requirements-dont-you-have.ingest.md:2:description: "Goedecke argues coding agents invent unrequested requirements such as mutexes, re-checks and consistency guards; stated tolerances and review that scans for added coordination are his repairs"
kb/sources/08-simplicity-hidden-in-complexity.ingest.md:2:description: "Compression as predictive objective, measurement instrument, and interface—plus its limits as a theory of generalization"
kb/sources/multi-agent-analytics-control-plane-2087241401649996149.ingest.md:2:description: "A practitioner redesign centralizes diagnostic authority while retaining fact-returning sub-agents, deterministic anomaly detection, and graph-bounded hypothesis traversal"
kb/sources/07-the-pivot-to-reasoning.ingest.md:2:description: "Reasoning architectures and runtime methods read through fixed decompositions, process validity, and benchmark turnover"
kb/sources/skilllift-dense-rubrics-sparse-oracles.ingest.md:2:description: "SkillLift learns textual rubrics from execution rankings to guide cheaper skill revision, supporting calibrated diagnostic feedback within task-specific search rather than general rubric reliability."
kb/sources/beyond-fixed-representations-vocabulary-verifier-gaps.ingest.md:2:description: "Conceptual paper separates primitive invention from adaptive evaluation, sharpening Commonplace's fixed-decomposition analysis while leaving its autonomy ladder untested."
kb/sources/awareness-requirements-adaptive-systems.ingest.md:2:description: "Awareness Requirements make requirement-state monitoring explicit, but leave goal authority, proxy validity and knowledge revision outside the demonstrated loop."
kb/sources/weco-first-evidence-recursive-self-improvement.ingest.md:2:description: "Weco reports fixed-model harness evolution with held-out task gains, diagnostic repairs and an inconclusive test of whether the evolved agent improves agents better."
kb/sources/envharness-awakening-static-worlds-for-agent-learning.ingest.md:2:description: "EnvHarness turns fixed benchmarks into policy-targeted training environments through interface wrappers, while its gains test a fixed wrapper and skill-extraction bundle rather than validating that decomposition."
kb/sources/meta-harness-end-to-end-optimization-of-model-harnesses.ingest.md:2:description: Controlled ablation showing raw execution traces (10 MTok/iter) outperform summaries by 10+ points in automated harness search — first empirical evidence for diagnostic richness as binding constraint
kb/sources/spade-self-play-in-adaptive-synthetic-executable-environments.ingest.md:2:description: "SPADE is a code-grounded case of adaptive executable-environment generation inside a fixed training decomposition, with released mechanisms but unreleased outcome artifacts at the pinned commit."
kb/sources/wg14-n1570-behavior-definitions.ingest.md:2:description: "N1570 distinguishes documented implementation choices, permitted alternatives and behavior without standard requirements, bounding claims about shared semantics and conformance."
kb/sources/requirements-aware-systems-research-agenda.ingest.md:2:description: "A 2010 research agenda extends requirements reflection into runtime model evolution, uncertainty, trade-offs, and explanation, supplying structural lineage rather than outcome evidence."
kb/sources/llm-webagents-long-context-reasoning-benchmark.ingest.md:2:description: "NeurIPS workshop study injects irrelevant prior tasks into web-agent contexts and observes soft degradation, loops, and objective loss, extending controlled distractor findings to multi-session agents"
kb/sources/nested-learning-the-illusion-of-deep-learning-architecture.ingest.md:2:description: "Nested Learning recasts architectures and optimizers as nested associative memories, but Hope's broad gains vary local components within a fixed weight-only decomposition"
kb/sources/last-ai-built-by-humans-recursive-self-improvement.ingest.md:2:description: "An RSI survey separates inherited improvement mechanisms from demonstrated improvement capacity, with bounded industrial evidence for persistent artifact adaptation."
kb/sources/requirements-reflection-runtime-entities.ingest.md:2:description: "A 2010 design proposal reifies requirements as runtime objects and synchronizes them with architecture, providing a structural precedent for causal self-representation without evidence of conjectural learning."
kb/sources/model-discovery-agent-bayesian-experiment-design.ingest.md:2:description: "MDA splits scientific model discovery between LLM hypothesis proposal and Bayesian selection, improving interventional forecasts inside a fixed domain decomposition"
kb/sources/no-neutral-harness-config-fragile-items.ingest.md:2:description: "A multiple-choice harness grid traces ranking changes to unstable items, supporting diagnostic prompt variation while limiting scoring attribution and robust-only comparisons."
kb/sources/harnessevolve-reference-trajectories.ingest.md:2:description: "HarnessEvolve adds answer-conditioned reference trajectories to harness diagnosis; its ablation supports diagnostic access within a fixed optimization and gating procedure."
kb/sources/acm-agentic-context-management-for-long-horizon-tasks.ingest.md:2:description: "ACM improves three benchmarks inside a fixed two-tool decomposition, but neither tests that decomposition's scope nor shows lossless active context"
kb/sources/agent-optimizers-compound-terminal-bench.ingest.md:2:description: "Two-phase optimizer study exposes transfer and re-optimization failures, but its compounding claim lacks a fresh-start causal control and rests on a fixed Terminal-Bench decomposition."
kb/sources/09-safe-superintelligence.ingest.md:2:description: "Operational intelligence measures and safety narratives tested against objectives, proxy warrant, and oracle domains"
kb/sources/long-horizon-agents-levels-ticks-cascaded-intelligence.ingest.md:2:description: "A ten-day agent campaign illustrates bounded live state, clocked execution and review-based escalation; its retained operating changes offer limited evidence of adaptation without weight updates."
kb/sources/arkenos-landing-page.ingest.md:2:description: "ArkenOS landing page claims self-improving research agent swarms with nightly 'dream' consolidation into shared memories and skills; claim without mechanism, objective, or metric"
kb/sources/decentralized-multi-agent-systems-with-shared-context.ingest.md:2:description: "DeLM's verified shared-state experiments support coordination guarantees and hierarchical context scheduling while leaving the fixed decomposition untested"
kb/sources/four-dark-corners-requirements-engineering.ingest.md:2:description: "Zave and Jackson ground requirements in environmental phenomena and derive implementable specifications using domain assumptions, without settling goal authority or assumption revision."
kb/sources/weyns-software-engineering-self-adaptive-systems-tour.ingest.md:2:description: "Weyns's six-wave engineering perspective supplies a bounded self-adaptation vocabulary and a warning that MAPE-K is an engineering reference model, not a membership definition."
kb/sources/machine-studying.ingest.md:2:description: "Machine Studying defines corpus-only pre-task adaptation and evaluates it across inference budgets, but its preliminary interventions and fixed StudyBench decomposition support narrower claims than the headline"
kb/sources/relax-uncertainty-self-adaptive-systems.ingest.md:2:description: "RELAX specifies stakeholder-bounded flexibility and monitoring assumptions for adaptive systems, without validating goals or demonstrating learned requirements revision."
kb/sources/effective-harnesses-for-long-running-agents.ingest.md:2:description: "Anthropic practitioner report separating context continuation from work continuation through persistent progress state, structured requirements, incremental commits, and end-to-end verification"
kb/sources/popper-conjectures-and-refutations.ingest.md:2:description: "Popper's account of knowledge growth through criticism adds independent-test and empirical-success requirements to Commonplace's analysis of claim repair."
kb/sources/workspace-optimization-how-to-train-your-agent.ingest.md:2:description: "DreamTeam adapts a fixed-model agent by revising typed code and role context from prediction failures, but does not isolate the value of its fixed workspace decomposition."
kb/sources/error-centric-intelligence-beyond-observational-learning.ingest.md:2:description: "Thomas proposes error-driven changes to hypothesis spaces and structural diagnostics for causal learning; the contribution is conceptual and does not establish that fixed-model systems cannot create knowledge."
kb/sources/eurisko-learns-new-heuristics-and-domain-concepts.ingest.md:2:description: "Lenat's EURISKO report links heuristic self-modification to representation, objective quality, credit assignment, and recurring human correction."

EXIT: 0
